It comes from how the three currently fit together, not from anything I changed. What I did:
- added the org's tables to the publication, using ardoq-api's own procedure;
- created the override that resets the sync consumer;
- ran a resync.

None of these touches Debezium's config or graphlake-sync's code, and the number format comes from those two.

My publication change is what made the live path run for ardoqbundlesproduction, so it's the first time the bug showed up here. Any org whose tables are in the publication goes through the same Debezium config and the same graphlake-sync code, so I'd expect the same result, but I haven't checked another org.

